module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.execution_provenance_loss

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data execution_provenance_loss: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "execution_provenance_loss" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**execution-provenance loss** (a reported value is consumed as though an observation produced it, while the carrier holds no proof the observation path ran. ",

    "**Distinct from state-space conflation, and the repair law is what separates them**: there the carrier cannot represent the distinction and the fix is to split the states; here the carrier already has the state — the consumer simply cannot tell whether it was *reached*, and the fix is to bind an execution receipt to the value. ",

    "Three specimens in one night, all on main, none of them a missing variant. ",

    "`known_red_held=206` is `36 held + 170 that RUNTIME-ERRORED`: the substrate splits those into distinct arms, so the states exist; what the quoted figure loses is *did the assertion run*, and an expected-red row that threw is not evidence the red is expected — it is a row whose assertion never executed. ",

    "A floor whose `TerminalLedgerUnrenderable` count is `0` reads identically whether the ledger checks passed or preparation refused before a ledger existed. ",

    "And a `.dag` board of `E0599=23 E0308=128` reads identically whether cargo ran or normalize refused upstream of it. ",

    "**The receipt that makes this worth a row rather than a caution:** for three hours after #8976 put a §4c-illegal annotation inside a match body, the compiler refused at strict preparation while downstream measurements kept producing valid-looking values — one lane concluded a defect was closed, another concluded the same defect was still firing, both citing runs where it could not appear at all; three separate A/B comparisons reported perfect agreement, one because both arms were broken identically, one because a missing flag meant no arm executed, and one because the defect had been fixed between runs so both arms were the same bytes. ",

    "Every one of those is downstream of a single fact: **a masked run and a clean run rendered identically.** Recognition rule: if a count of zero and an unreached stage produce the same output, the number is not an observation. ",

    "The construction move, and it is stronger than naming known masks because it also forecloses the undiscovered ones: any stage capable of preventing a downstream observation from executing must participate in the observation carrier, so `refused before stage N` cannot inhabit the same carrier as `stage N executed with zero findings` — a known mask is a hole someone found, execution provenance is what stops an unfound hole from masquerading as a measurement.)",
    "**A HUMAN-SIDE SPECIMEN, AND ITS ORIGIN IS A MECHANISM RATHER THAN A LOOSE PROXY (2026-09-04/05, gunbc#10490 / gunbc#10491).** A reviewer offered a matched pair as evidence for a failure-mode row: a RED arm at head c30c049f68 and a GREEN arm at head 5888fb0106 after integrating main. The red arm was executed and real. The green arm was never queried. What was actually read was the TREE at that head -- the function present, and git merge-base --is-ancestor of the commit that added it true -- and that property was reported as the job result. THE TIMES, because the adjective is not the finding: the message asserting the green arm was sent 00:19:10Z; heal-generated-artifacts on 5888fb0106 STARTED 00:18:32Z and COMPLETED 00:35:42Z. Sixteen minutes early, and the row it was offered for was about misattributed evidence, so accepting it would have reproduced the class inside its own filing. It was refused at intake and gunbc#10479 at 245416762b -- where heal actually ran and passed in 18m56s after exactly the prescribed remedy -- was substituted as the executed control. ",

    "**WHY THAT SUBSTITUTION IS THE HARD CASE OF THIS ROW: the tree property is CAUSALLY UPSTREAM of the green, not an unrelated proxy.** It is the actual mechanism by which the job passes, which is what made reading it feel like verification rather than prediction -- a proxy known to be loose gets checked, and a mechanism believed gets reported. Every ordinary defence here fails: the reasoning was correct, the measurement was correct, the prediction was correct, and the claim was still unbacked, because the proposition asserted was about a JOB and the evidence held was about a TREE. ",

    "**AND IT COMPLETED SUCCESS, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THE CLASS EXPENSIVE RATHER THAN EMBARRASSING.** Afterwards a lucky prediction and a verified control are indistinguishable: nothing goes red, and re-checking reproduces the same true-of-nothing answer. Had it failed, the row would have carried a false positive control and nothing in the offer would have warned the reader. That asymmetry is the one receipt_names_a_property_not_the_tree_it_holds_of records for expired greens -- same shape, different subject: there a green stops being true when its base moves, here a green was never observed at all. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE, AND THE SPECIMEN CARRIES ITS OWN WARNING ABOUT IT: name the observation you queried, not the state that implies it.** This row was offered by that same reviewer as the candidate identity for the OTHER lane's class twenty minutes earlier, read carefully, and correctly judged a poor fit there -- and was not recognised when the next error was their own. Reading a class is not detecting it; the question that would have caught it is mechanical and takes one call: WHICH API DID I QUERY FOR THIS OUTCOME. If the answer names a file, a commit, an ancestry test or a diff, the outcome is predicted and must be reported as a prediction. ",

  ],

  evidence: [],
}
